'''Bodhisattva Cat''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]]. It was added in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 5.0 Update|Version 5.0]] increases range and gains the ability to [[Weaken|weaken]] [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. [[Talents]] were added in [[Version 8.0 Update|Version 8.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 30
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Bodhisattva Cat
|name2 = Avalokitesvara Cat
|name3 = Tathagata Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Avalokitesvara Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Tathagata Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bodhisattva Cat would be a solid anti-Floating unit if not for the existence of [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], whose True Form, Sanzo Cat, does everything Bodhisattva Cat does and more. Bodhisattva may have higher stats, but when it comes to stalling Floating enemies, there's just no beating Sanzo's spammability.

If Sanzo Cat is not owned, Bodhisattva Cat can be stacked to effectively counter [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Buns]], [[Shy Boy]]s and some of the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s. Just don't invest too much into it, because it's only a matter of time until the [[Cat Capsule|Rare Cat Capsules]] blesses you with Bishop Cat.

==='''True Form'''===
Tathagata Cat gains more health, along with more range. All of this increases its general use, and it now fully outranges [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]], although this is still very situational if you have [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]]. Beyond that, it is still outclassed by Sanzo and Necro-Dancer, both of whom remain more spammable than Tathagata Cat. Furthermore, as the slow chance has not increased, Tathagata Cat is still unreliable unless stacked. At the very least, Tathagata Cat is a decent substitute in situations where Sanzo is outranged, which only a few notable Floating enemies do: [[Mooth]], [[Maawth]] and [[Owlbrow]].

==='''Talents'''===
Even with [[Talents]], Tathagata Cat will never be able to reach the standards of Sanzo Cat, who ends up having the same exact abilities, so there is no real reason to invest in it.

Move Speed Up is situational and not recommended, as it may sometimes cause Tathagata Cat to creep into the range of dangerous enemies and die horribly as a result. Health Buff is also not recommended, as Tathagata Cat, despite having decent stats, won't go anywhere with only two knockbacks, a long recharge time and little more to give it value. The same goes for Attack Buff, unless you're desperate for a new ranged attacker. Even then, Tathagata Cat's range is not enough to deal with most late-game enemies, so you won't lose much by not investing in it.

However, there are two Talents that aren't complete disappointments: Weaken and Slow Up. Both of these allow its effects to last beyond their duration between attacks, which allows Tathagata Cat to almost perma-slow when stacked, and perma-weaken as well, to a lesser extent.

==='''Orb'''===
Tathagata Cat is not worth using any Talent Orbs on, however Attack Up VS. Floating is the best choice thanks to its moderately high AP.

