==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Bodhisattva Cat's slow chance from 10% to 40%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Avalokitesvara Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Dharma (Removed Combo)|Dharma]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Bodhisattva Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Bodhisattva Cat
A Cat that has reached a state of peace
and pushed its body beyond physical limits.
Might slow Floating enemies (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Avalokitesvara Cat
A Bodhisattva Cat who has shown
compassion to many and all Battle Cats.
Might slow Floating enemies (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Tathagata Cat
Enlightened compassion flows from this Cat.
But they say even the Buddha has a breaking
point. Area attacks might weaken/slow Floating.</pre>
*In Buddhism, a [[wikipedia:Bodhisattva|bodhisattva]] is someone who is able to reach nirvana but chooses not to do so in order to help others attain enlightenment.
**[[wikipedia:Avalokiteśvara|Avalokiteśvara]] (meaning "The Lord Who Looks Down [with compassion]") is a many-armed bodhisattva who embodies the compassion of all Buddhas.
**[[wikipedia:Tathāgata|Tathāgata]] is an honorific title of a Buddha; the historical Buddha, Siddhārtha Gautama, would often refer to himself as ''the Tathāgata'' instead of using any personal pronouns. The meaning of this word is unknown, but is widely believed to be "one who has thus gone" or "one who has thus come".
*Even though Avalokitesvara Cat's hands attack at different times, it wasn't updated to have multi-hit in [[Version 6.0 Update|version 6.0]].

